      "title": "Natco Pharma Q1 results: Profit falls 57% to ₹206 cr, revenue at ₹735 cr",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/natco-pharma-q1-results-profit-falls-57-to-206-cr-revenue-at-735-cr-126081401116_1.html",
      "description": "Natco Pharma Ltd on Friday reported a 57 per cent decline in consolidated net profit at Rs 206.5 crore in the first quarter ended June 2026, hit by lower sales of its generic cancer treatment drug lenalidomide.\nThe company had posted a consolidated net profit of Rs 480.3 crore in the corresponding quarter last fiscal, Natco Pharma said in a regulatory filing.\nConsolidated revenue from operations in the first quarter was lower at Rs 735.2 crore in the first quarter as compared to Rs 1,328.9 crore in the corresponding period a year ago, it added.\nThe decline is largely attributable to lower lenalidomide revenue in the current quarter, which was partially offset by growth in the base business, the company said.\nTotal expenses in the quarter under review were lower at Rs 608.8 crore as compared to Rs 818.7 crore in the same period a year ago, it added.\nIn the first quarter, domestic pharmaceutical formulations revenue was at Rs 136.4 crore, up from Rs 107 crore in the year-ago period.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-14T10:13:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "Ashok Leyland Q1FY27 results: Net profit rises 1.5% to ₹667.77 crore",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/ashok-leyland-q1fy27-results-net-profit-rises-1-5-to-667-77-crore-126081400997_1.html",
      "description": "Commercial vehicle maker Ashok Leyland Ltd on Friday reported a 1.5 per cent increase in consolidated net profit at Rs 667.77 crore for the first quarter ended June 30, 2026.\nThe company had posted a consolidated net profit of Rs 657.72 crore in the corresponding period of the previous fiscal, Ashok Leyland Ltd said in a regulatory filing.\nConsolidated revenue from operations stood at Rs 13,069.59 crore in the quarter under review as against Rs 11,708.54 crore in the year-ago period, it added.\nThe company's board has approved an investment of up to 25 million pounds (approximately Rs 325 crore) in its UK subsidiary Optare Plc. and another up to Rs 500 crore in equity shares of Hinduja Housing Finance Ltd through secondary purchase of shares.\nTotal expenses in the quarter under review were higher at Rs 12,314.66 crore as compared to Rs 10,920.53 crore in the same period a year ago, the company said.\nDuring the quarter, the company said it posted its highest ever commercial vehicles",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-14T08:38:19"
    }
